# Secrets for `pnpm lab:add` (uploads poster / mp4 to R2). docs/setup.md
#
# EVERY MACHINE NEEDS ITS OWN .env — it is gitignored and never committed, so cloning the repo does not bring it.
# On a new machine:  cp .env.example .env  and fill in the values below.
# Only `pnpm lab:add` reads it. new / dev:lab / lab:build / dev / preview / Pages deploys work without it.
#
# Where the values come from: Cloudflare dashboard → R2 → Manage API tokens → token "takumifukasawa-media-lab-add"
# (Object Read & Write, bucket takumifukasawa-media only). The secret is shown only once; if it is lost,
# delete the token and create a new one with the same settings.

# S3 endpoint shown with the token: https://<account id>.r2.cloudflarestorage.com
R2_ENDPOINT=
R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
R2_BUCKET=takumifukasawa-media
